    "snippet": "RESPONSE TO QUESTION SUBMITTED BY MR. GIMENEZ Mr. Gimenez. Where does the role of AI play out in the Army's Modernization Strategy? How important will AI be in the next war? How are you budgeting and accounting for this technology for the fight tomorrow, in 10 years, and for the Army of 2040? Secretary Wormuth. AI will...",
    "full_text": "RESPONSE TO QUESTION SUBMITTED BY MR. GIMENEZ Mr. Gimenez. Where does the role of AI play out in the Army's Modernization Strategy? How important will AI be in the next war? How are you budgeting and accounting for this technology for the fight tomorrow, in 10 years, and for the Army of 2040? Secretary Wormuth. AI will play an integrating role in Army capability modernization and transformation efforts. Whether it is through automation of workflows and gaining efficiencies for Army capabilities as we transform in contact. Or through reducing cognitive and physical burdens through employing Human Machine Integrated Formations and AI enabled command and coordination as we conduct deliberate transformation. Or even aligning AI concepts and capabilities into the design of concept driven transformation, AI will integrate with and enhance the abilities of Commanders and the formations they lead to understand themselves and our adversaries, and act on the massive amounts of data that drive their decisions and actions at speed. This manifests through investing in digital transformation and the modernization of the Army's underlying network and computer infrastructure. These investments will allow the Army to take advantage of machine learning, AI technologies, and applications to understand, visualize, decide, and direct faster than our competitors. AI will be relevant to the next war as evidenced by what we are seeing in current conflicts and broad industry and societal adoption. AI is enabling the gathering and processing of information at speeds beyond human capacity and distances beyond physical line of sight enabling employment of robotic and autonomous systems in ways that are preserving the Army's ability to employ our most important capability, the Soldier in a manner that retains the ability of the commander to align human effort to the things that humans are proficient at and machines to those tasks that they are suited for. The Army is focused on delivering AI solutions at the speed and place of relevance, so that commanders can make informed, ethical decisions while staying ahead of competitors. The Army is aligning resourcing to efforts that are enabling exploration and demonstration of how the Army will integrate AI into modernization and efforts to transform formations. We are seeing the fusion of AI into capabilities ranging from the strategic support area to formations at the tactical edge. Experimentation and study efforts will harvest the best approaches and associated materiel and nonmateriel capabilities for incorporation into the design of the future force. ______"
